      "writtenOn": "2022-09-19T23:52:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems like too big of a hammer for this problem, since we can force shutdown in situtations that are probably still relevant to debug mode (like if a regulator falls out of tolerance). How exactly do the signals get lost? Should debug mode stop monitoring the SLP_S* lines and continue operating the others normally?",
      "revId": "b925cac46b0a4d281dc5766effa24476d1acaf3e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b386aa3_e7301277",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1296157
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-20T00:01:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When the BOOTHALT# is driven low by the debugger, platform reset can happen and eSPI may reset. EC will not be able to get SX lines in given time, thus EC will put AP in G3. This console option gives flexibility for the user to bypass such situations",
      "parentUuid": "c9e82cb1_611a8b48",
      "revId": "b925cac46b0a4d281dc5766effa24476d1acaf3e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aeec2856_6f36e248",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-20T01:18:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Then I don\u0027t think we want to completely block apshutdown in that configuration; debug mode should probably then make the power state machine ignore the affected signals from the AP, and resync when debug mode is disabled. Otherwise the power state machine will probably end up in an unpredictable state, and we\u0027d be blocking some uses of apshutdown that are still meaningful even in debug mode.",
      "parentUuid": "1b386aa3_e7301277",
      "revId": "b925cac46b0a4d281dc5766effa24476d1acaf3e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3d2d0f5d_71dce49f",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1296157
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-20T01:27:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "by default ap_debug is disabled. User will enable/disable it only when they plug in the debugger. As AP debug is independent of EC, it is difficult to synchronize and predict the states.\nEX: Lets say if we step through way before PMC (eSPI IP) starts, then EC not even receive SX signals until eSPI IP gets initialized.",
      "parentUuid": "aeec2856_6f36e248",
      "revId": "b925cac46b0a4d281dc5766effa24476d1acaf3e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
